{
  "slug": "js_json_syntax",
  "course": "js",
  "order": 168,
  "url": "/js/js_json_syntax.asp",
  "title": "JavaScript JSON Syntax",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JavaScript JSON Syntax"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JSON has a very simple syntax for representing structured data."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "One JSON document consists of one JSON value."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The value can be:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["An Object", "An Array", "A String", "A Number", "A Boolean", "or null"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JSON Object Literals"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "This is a JSON string:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "'{\"name\":\"John\", \"age\":30, \"car\":null}'",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Inside the JSON string there is a JSON object literal:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "{\"name\":\"John\", \"age\":30, \"car\":null}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A JSON object is written between curly braces { }."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "An object contains zero or more properties."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Properties comes in key/value pairs separated by commas."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "key names are strings enclosed in double quotes."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Keys and values are separated by a colon."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Values must be a valid JSON data type. JSON supports six value types:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        ["Value", "Example"],
        ["String", "\"John\""],
        ["Number", "42"],
        ["Boolean", "true"],
        ["Null", "null"],
        ["Object", "{\"name\" : \"John\"}"],
        ["Array", "[1, 2, 3]"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "It is a common mistake to call a JSON object literal \"a JSON object\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JSON cannot be an object. JSON is a string format."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The data is only JSON when it is in a string format."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "When a JSON object litteral is converted into a JavaScript variable, it becomes a JavaScript object."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "JSON Array Literals"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "This is a JSON string:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "'[\"Ford\", \"BMW\", \"Fiat\"]'",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Inside the JSON string there is a JSON array literal:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "[\"Ford\", \"BMW\", \"Fiat\"]",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "[\n\n  \"Apple\",\n\n  \"Banana\",\n\n  \"Orange\"\n\n]",
      "caption": "Other Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "[1, 2, 3, 4 ,5]",
      "caption": "Other Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A JSON array is written between square brackets [ ]."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "An array contains zero or more values."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Values are separated by commas."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Values can be any of the six JSON data types:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        ["Value", "Example"],
        ["String", "\"John\""],
        ["Number", "42"],
        ["Boolean", "true"],
        ["Null", "null"],
        ["Object", "{\"name\" : \"John\"}"],
        ["Array", "[1, 2, 3]"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JSON syntax is derived from JavaScript object notation syntax:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Curly braces hold objects",
        "Properties comes is in name/value pairs",
        "Properties are separated by commas",
        "Square brackets hold arrays",
        "Strings are in double quotes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "But, JSON has stricter syntax rules than JavaScript objects."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "JSON Does Not Allow"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JSON has a small, strict syntax."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The following JavaScript features are not valid JSON:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        ["Feature", "JSON", "JS"],
        ["Unquoted property names", "No", "Yes"],
        ["Single quoted strings", "No", "Yes"],
        ["Trailing commas", "No", "Yes"],
        ["Comments", "No", "Yes"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "JSON Property Names"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Every property name must be a string."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Property names must be enclosed in double quotes."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "{\n\n  \"name\": \"John\"\n\n}",
      "caption": "Valid:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "{\n\n  name: \"John\"\n\n}",
      "caption": "Valid:"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "JSON Strings"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JSON strings must use double quotes."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "{\n\n  \"city\": \"London\"\n\n}",
      "caption": "Valid:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "{\n\n  \"city\": 'London'\n\n}",
      "caption": "Valid:"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Whitespace"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Whitespace is ignored outside strings."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can use spaces, tabs, and line breaks to make JSON easier to read."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "{\"name\":\"John\", \"age\":30}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "{\n\n  \"name\": \"John\",\n\n  \"age\": 30\n\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Trailing Commas"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JSON does not allow a comma after the last property or array value."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "{\n\n  \"name\": \"John\",\n\n  \"age\": 30,\n\n}",
      "caption": "Wrong:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "{\n\n  \"name\": \"John\",\n\n  \"age\": 30\n\n}",
      "caption": "Wrong:"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Comments Are Not Allowed"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JSON does not support comments."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "{\n\n  // Customer name\n\n  \"name\": \"John\"\n\n}",
      "caption": "Wrong"
    }
  ]
}
